[heading]About this mod[/heading]

[b]Travel Between Visited Traders[/b] adds a trader dialog option that lets you travel back to traders you have already visited.

Talk to a trader once to record it for the current save. After that, choose [b]Travel to a visited trader[/b] in trader dialog and pick a destination from the list.

For normal single-player use, install the mod and leave the defaults alone.

[line]

[heading]Main features[/heading]

[list]
[*]Travel back to any trader you have already visited
[*]Destination list shows trader name, distance, direction, coordinates, access mode, and travel cost
[*]A short full-screen transport animation with departure and arrival messages
[*]Optional distance-based travel cost, such as gas or casino money (free by default)
[*]Long destination lists are split into pages
[*]Recognized vanilla and Wasteland Mod trader names are shown cleanly
[*]English and Japanese supported
[*]Works in single-player and multiplayer, with Personal / Party / Shared access modes for servers
[*]Prepares distant or unloaded trader areas before travel, and cancels the trip if the destination is not ready
[/list]

[line]

[heading]Installation[/heading]

Extract the [b]VisitedTraderTeleport[/b] folder into:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport
[/quote]

Requires the vanilla [b]0_TFP_Harmony[/b] mod included with current 7 Days to Die versions.

[b]Anti-cheat must be disabled for this DLL mod.[/b]

For multiplayer, install the mod on both the server and every client.

[line]

[heading]Access modes[/heading]

[b]Personal[/b] - travel only to traders you visited yourself (default).
[b]Party[/b] - also travel to traders visited by your current party members.
[b]Shared[/b] - any trader visited by anyone on the server is available to everyone.

In multiplayer, the server controls access, travel cost, and teleport validation.

[line]

[heading]Configuration[/heading]

All settings are in:

[quote]
7 Days To Die\Mods\VisitedTraderTeleport\Config\VisitedTraderTeleport.xml
[/quote]

For multiplayer, edit this on the server. Restart the game, host, or dedicated server after changing it.

[b]Access mode[/b]

[quote]
<AccessMode value="personal" />
[/quote]

Use [b]personal[/b], [b]party[/b], or [b]shared[/b].

[b]Travel cost[/b] (free by default)

[quote]
<TravelCost enabled="false" item="ammoGasCan" perMeter="0.1" minimum="0" />
[/quote]

[list]
[*][b]enabled[/b] - set to [b]true[/b] to charge for travel.
[*][b]item[/b] - the item to consume. Default is gas ([b]ammoGasCan[/b]); use [b]casinoCoin[/b] for Duke's casino tokens, or any item name.
[*][b]perMeter[/b] - amount charged per meter. For example, 0.1 is one item per 10 meters; 0.001 is one item per kilometer.
[*][b]minimum[/b] - the lowest cost for any paid trip.
[*][b]displayName[/b] - optional fallback name for the cost item, only needed for custom items that have no localized name in the game.
[/list]

[b]Travel transition[/b] (enabled by default)

[quote]
<TravelTransition enabled="true" durationSeconds="5" sound="suv_startup" soundRepeatSeconds="2" />
[/quote]

[list]
[*][b]enabled[/b] - set to [b]false[/b] for instant travel with no animation.
[*][b]durationSeconds[/b] - how long the animation is shown.
[*][b]sound[/b] - sound played during travel. Leave empty to turn it off.
[*][b]soundRepeatSeconds[/b] - how often the sound repeats. Set to 0 to play it once.
[/list]

[b]Travel confirmation[/b]

[quote]
<Confirmation mode="whenCost" />
[/quote]

Ask before traveling so a misclick does not send you (and your travel-cost items) somewhere by accident.

[list]
[*][b]off[/b] - travel immediately when you pick a destination.
[*][b]always[/b] - always show a [b]Travel to X?[/b] prompt with Yes/No.
[*][b]whenCost[/b] - ask only when the trip costs items; free trips stay instant. This is the default.
[/list]

Confirmation is a per-player setting read from each player's own config, so in multiplayer everyone chooses it for themselves.

[line]

[heading]Upgrading[/heading]

[b]You do not need to reset your save when upgrading.[/b] Existing visited-trader data is kept and loaded automatically, and new visits are saved going forward.

[line]

[heading]Notes[/heading]

[list]
[*]The current trader is not shown as a destination
[*]If there are no valid destinations, the screen explains none are available in the current mode
[*]Teleport destinations use the position saved when the trader visit was recorded
[*]If a destination cannot be prepared in time, travel is cancelled instead of forcing you into an unsafe area
[/list]
